  "details": "Hey VRChat Team,\n\nHope you’re all doing well! I wanted to suggest adding a personal messaging system to VRChat. With the recent removal of the \"boop\" feature, it feels like there's a gap that needs filling.\n\nHere’s why I think a messaging system would be awesome:\n\n1. Natural Evolution of Existing Systems:\n\nPeople are already using the request and invite systems to send messages. It's clear there's a need for this, and I bet even you guys have used it this way. The pieces are there; they just need to be put together better.\n\n2. Less Intrusive and More Meaningful:\n\nUnlike the boop system, which could be flashy and intrusive, messaging is about actual communication. Messages are personal and can be easily managed—blocked or removed if needed. Pokes were unnecessary and often disliked; messaging is more practical and appreciated.\n\n3. Enhances Authentic Social Interaction:\n\nWhile VRChat is all about in-person communication, limiting other forms can take away from the experience. Real life includes various ways to communicate, and adding messaging would make interactions more realistic and less pressured, especially for those with social anxiety.\n\n4. Accessibility Across Platforms:\n\nNot all users have an easy way to communicate outside VRChat. Using a browser on Quest or Pico can be a hassle and prone to crashes due to RAM issues. A built-in messaging system would provide a seamless way to communicate without relying on external platforms or devices, making things smoother for everyone.\n\nI really think adding a personal messaging system would fill the new void left by the boop feature and improve the social experience in VRChat. It would make connecting with friends more meaningful and convenient.\n\nThanks for considering this! Looking forward to your thoughts, or whatever alternative systems you provide eventually.",
